course: dictionary
lesson: 13825
title: Words with more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one fits. The word issuing is one of them. In «The librarian is issuing books to the pupils», issuing means giving out or officially handing something over. Try the meaning in the sentence to check it.
explain: In «The weather service is issuing a warning for storms», issuing means officially making something public. The warning is told to everyone, not handed to one person. The words around it, weather and warning, are the clues.
explain: Issuing can also mean coming or flowing out, as in «Thick grey smoke was issuing from the dragon's nose.» This is a more formal use. The smoke is not being given to anyone; it is pouring out. Ask yourself: what is being issued, a book, a warning, or smoke?
fact: Issuing is a form of the verb issue: issue, issues, issued, issuing.
fact: «Issuing» can mean giving out or officially supplying something, such as tickets or passports.
fact: «Issuing» can mean officially making something public, such as a warning or a statement.
fact: «Issuing» can also mean coming or flowing out, as in «smoke issuing from a chimney»; this use is formal or old.
exercise: «The librarian is issuing books to the pupils.» What is the librarian doing? | Throwing the books away | Reading the books aloud to the class | *Giving out books officially
exercise: «The weather service is issuing a warning for storms.» What does issuing mean here? | Singing a song about the storm | *Officially making the warning public | Hiding the warning from everyone
exercise: «Thick smoke was issuing from the dragon's nose.» What does issuing mean here? | Giving out tickets to the crowd | Falling fast asleep | *Coming or flowing out
test: «The office is issuing new passports this week.» What does issuing mean? | Shouting | Losing | Painting | *Officially giving out
test: «The school is issuing a statement about the trip.» What does issuing mean here? | Hiding | Sleeping | Tearing | *Officially making public
exam: Mia reads, «Smoke was issuing from the old chimney.» Which meaning fits best? | Officially making a warning public | Lending books to pupils | Giving out tickets | *Coming or flowing out
